From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tatsuki Tanaka <tatsuki@tanakatatsuki.dev>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 01:47:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sc8280xp: use 32-bit slots on MI2S backends

Speaker amps on MI2S (AW88261/AW88263S on xiaomi-marble) are set up
for 32-bit slots with BCLK = 64 * fs.

---
 sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
index 98b15a527e..a9974399f6 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
@@ -82,6 +82,12 @@ static int sc8280xp_be_hw_params_fixup(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd,
 	channels->min = 2;
 	channels->max = 2;
 	switch (cpu_dai->id) {
+	case PRIMARY_MI2S_RX...QUATERNARY_MI2S_TX:
+	case QUINARY_MI2S_RX...QUINARY_MI2S_TX:
+		/* Smart amps such as AW88261 expect 32-bit slots (BCLK = 64 * fs) */
+		snd_mask_none(fmt);
+		snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S32_LE);
+		break;
 	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_0:
 	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_1:
 	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_2:
